          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 52.2,
          "end": 54.372,
          "en": "So, in my case, GradientContainer,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 54.372,
          "end": 57.363,
          "en": "and add opening and closing parentheses thereafter.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 58.32,
          "end": 61.32,
          "en": "Now, you could add opening and closing curly braces.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 61.32,
          "end": 63.36,
          "en": "So, you add this like a method,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 63.36,
          "end": 65.37,
          "en": "just without a return value,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 65.37,
          "end": 67.71,
          "en": "but other than that, you added like a method.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 67.71,
          "end": 72.71000000000001,
          "en": "And then here, you could do some initialization work.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 73.17,
          "end": 74.003,
          "en": "This, by the way,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 74.003,
          "end": 77.46000000000001,
          "en": "is a comment which can be added with two forward slashes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 77.46000000000001,
          "end": 80.60300000000001,
          "en": "and which allows you to add some comment text",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 80.60300000000001,
          "end": 83.16,
          "en": "which will not be interpreted as code,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 83.16,
          "end": 84.3,
          "en": "but which will be ignored,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 84.3,
          "end": 87.15,
          "en": "but which can help other developers understand your code.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 88.02,
          "end": 89.78999999999999,
          "en": "So, this is how you could add a constructor",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 89.78999999999999,
          "end": 91.59,
          "en": "and do some initialization work,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 91.59,
          "end": 96.09,
          "en": "though often you won't even need to add these curly braces.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 96.09,
          "end": 98.82,
          "en": "Instead, here, to get rid of these blue squiggly lines,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 98.82,
          "end": 101.55799999999999,
          "en": "you just have to accept a special named parameter",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 101.55799999999999,
          "end": 103.904,
          "en": "as part of your GradientContainer.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 103.904,
          "end": 107.91,
          "en": "And you do that by adding opening and closing curly braces.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 107.91,
          "end": 109.959,
          "en": "This is how in any function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 109.959,
          "end": 113.104,
          "en": "you can accept named arguments.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 113.104,
          "end": 115.71000000000001,
          "en": "Positional arguments are accepted",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 115.71000000000001,
          "end": 118.92,
          "en": "by simply adding a comma-separated list of parameters.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 118.92,
          "end": 122.07,
          "en": "Named arguments or parameters are accepted",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 122.07,
          "end": 125.49,
          "en": "by using curly braces around that list.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 125.49,
          "end": 126.66,
          "en": "And then here, for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 126.66,
          "end": 127.68,
          "en": "A and B would be",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 127.68,
          "end": 131.04,
          "en": "the names of the arguments you wanna accept.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 131.04,
          "end": 133.572,
          "en": "But here, it's a special argument named key,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 133.572,
          "end": 135.437,
          "en": "which you should accept.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 135.437,
          "end": 137.82,
          "en": "And this key argument, in the end,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 137.82,
          "end": 140.46,
          "en": "needs to be forwarded to StatelessWidget.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 140.46,
          "end": 142.657,
          "en": "So, this widget from which we are inheriting,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 142.657,
          "end": 146.91,
          "en": "which we are extending, wants a key argument,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 146.91,
          "end": 148.29,
          "en": "and that's why your class",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 148.29,
          "end": 150.54,
          "en": "should accept such a key argument as well",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 150.54,
          "end": 153.27,
          "en": "and forward it to StatelessWidget.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 153.27,
          "end": 156.21,
          "en": "Now, to forward it, you have two main options.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 156.21,
          "end": 160.504,
          "en": "You can add a colon after your constructor function name",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 160.504,
          "end": 162.9,
          "en": "and the parentheses,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 162.9,
          "end": 164.37,
          "en": "and then thereafter,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 164.37,
          "end": 167.566,
          "en": "you can do some variable initialization work,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 167.566,
          "end": 169.702,
          "en": "which sounds strange,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 169.702,
          "end": 173.52,
          "en": "also because we haven't learned a lot about variables yet.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 173.52,
          "end": 176.175,
          "en": "But here, you can reach out to the parent class",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 176.175,
          "end": 178.53,
          "en": "from which you are inheriting",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 178.53,
          "end": 181.326,
          "en": "by using another special keyword built into Dart,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 181.326,
          "end": 185.49099999999999,
          "en": "the super keyword, executed like a function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 185.49099999999999,
          "end": 188.82,
          "en": "Effectively, this is calling the constructor function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 188.82,
          "end": 191.25,
          "en": "of the parent class then.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 191.25,
          "end": 194.931,
          "en": "And here, you must set the named key argument",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 194.931,
          "end": 197.94,
          "en": "to your key here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 197.94,
          "end": 199.41,
          "en": "which is why I'm repeating key.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 199.41,
          "end": 203.31,
          "en": "This key here is referring to my named argument called Key.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 203.31,
          "end": 205.41,
          "en": "The first key in front of the colon",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 205.41,
          "end": 207.78,
          "en": "is referring to a named argument called key",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 207.78,
          "end": 210.665,
          "en": "in the super class in the Stateless-Widget class.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 210.665,
          "end": 214.23,
          "en": "This would be one way of forwarding this key argument,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 214.23,
          "end": 215.79,
          "en": "which is what you should do here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 215.79,
          "end": 217.86,
          "en": "But since you need to do this quite often,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 217.86,
          "end": 220.17000000000002,
          "en": "basically for all your widget classes,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 220.17000000000002,
          "end": 222.869,
          "en": "and this is a bit verbose if you write it like this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 222.869,
          "end": 225.75,
          "en": "Dart also gives you a shortcut.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 225.75,
          "end": 229.29,
          "en": "You can simply write super.key here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 229.29,
          "end": 232.41,
          "en": "and this will accept a named argument called key",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 232.41,
          "end": 235.02,
          "en": "and automatically forward it to the super class,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 235.02,
          "end": 237.81,
          "en": "so to StatelessWidget under that same name,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 237.81,
          "end": 240.27,
          "en": "so also under the name key.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 240.27,
          "end": 242.82,
          "en": "And that is something you should do here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 242.82,
          "end": 245.43,
          "en": "Now, I also got some more blue squiggly lines here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 245.43,
          "end": 246.263,
          "en": "where in the end,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 246.263,
          "end": 249.87,
          "en": "I learned that I should turn this into a const constructor",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 249.87,
          "end": 252.54,
          "en": "by adding const in front of it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 252.54,
          "end": 256.08,
          "en": "And this is a place where we haven't used const before.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 256.08,
          "end": 258.443,
          "en": "We only used it in front of values,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 258.443,
          "end": 261.51,
          "en": "but in the end, when we used it in front of values,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 261.51,
          "end": 264.39,
          "en": "we took advantage of constructor functions",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 264.39,
          "end": 267.75,
          "en": "that had this const annotation internally.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 267.75,
          "end": 269.58,
          "en": "When defining your own classes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 269.58,
          "end": 271.62,
          "en": "with your own constructor functions,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 271.62,
          "end": 274.86,
          "en": "you often can add const in front of them",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 274.86,
          "end": 276.78,
          "en": "to tell Dart that this in the end,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 276.78,
          "end": 279.84000000000003,
          "en": "is a class that can be optimized,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 279.84000000000003,
          "end": 283.499,
          "en": "that can be stored in memory such that it is reused,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 283.499,
